  "id": "kindling",
  "term": "kindling",
  "definition": "In the context of alcohol withdrawal, kindling is the idea that earlier episodes of complicated withdrawal make a later withdrawal episode more likely to become complicated as well. It describes how a person’s withdrawal history can strongly influence current risk.",
